{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "The Rice Cookout"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Kitchen Innovations"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 18}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Exchange advice and suggestions in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The First Conditional vs. The Second Conditional"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p>You use the first conditional to talk about real situations in the the present of future.</p>You use the second conditional to talk about unreal or imaginary (hypothetical) situations in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "First conditional form:<br/>If + Simple Present verb, + will<br/><span class=\"italic\">If you come over, I'll help you with that.</span><br/>(you can come over)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Second conditional form:<br/>If + Simple Past verb, + would<br/> <span class=\"italic\">If you had time, I would help you with that.</span><br/>(I don't think or I know you don't have time)"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">First Conditional<br/>(Cause and Effect)</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Second Conditional<br/>(Hypothetical Situations)</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><p>If you come in, you can look over our services.</p><p>If you engage us, you are tapping into a service that will make your life easier!</p><p>Our friendly employees will be here to help you if you are ready.</p><p>If you come in next week, you can take advantage of our sale.</p><p>If you aren't satisfied, we'll give you a full refund.</p></span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><p>If you could have someone else do up your meal, would you be interested?</p><p>If you had time to relax before the big night, you'd feel rested.</p><p>If you ever thought you needed a cooking alternative, you should have a look.</p><p>If you wanted to plan a party today, we could help.</p><p>If you wanted to talk to one of our satisfied customers, we could arrange that.</p></span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Remember to use a comma (,) after the <span class=\"italic\">IF</span> clause."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In conversation, it is common to use contractions. (<span class=\"italic\">I would</span> = <span class=\"italic\">I'd</span>)"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Future With <span class=\"italic\">Will</span>, <span class=\"italic\">Going to</span>, the Present Continuous"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use three different tenses to talk about the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you talk about things that are not decided or when you make a decision at the moment of speaking for the future, you use the modal <span class=\"italic\">will</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you ask about intentions, you use <span class=\"italic\">be going to</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you talk about things that are arranged, on the agenda or booked for the future, you use the Present Continuous tense."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Will</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Will the meal turn out just right?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Going to</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Are you going to stand at the stove all day?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present Continuous</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Are you having people over for dinner soon?</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "We at Kitchen Innovations will take your cooking troubles away."}, {"type": "example", "content": "When you engage us, you are tapping into a service that will make your life easier!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Our friendly employees will be here to help you."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You're going to find them polite, courteous and helpful."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Starting next week, we're offering a discount so don't hesitate."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to do up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to create; to package; to put together"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You could have someone else do up your meal!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le18ob05aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear when you listen to an offer."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "innovation"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a new way to do something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We at Kitchen Innovations will take your cooking troubles away."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le18ob05aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "courteous"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "polite"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Our staff is courteous and helpful."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le18ob05aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "overcooked"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "cooked too much"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: No more overcooked vegetables!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le18ob05aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to rustle up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to prepare; to cook"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"},